.TH LIBMPQ__UPDATE_REPLACE_PATH 3 2026-09-25 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__update_replace_path \- replace a named member from a filesystem path
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__update_replace_path(mpq_update_s *update, const char *filename, const char *source_path, const mpq_file_options_s *options);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads replacement bytes from \fIsource_path\fP and replaces the existing \fIfilename\fP in the private working copy. Optional \fIoptions\fP use the same writer storage semantics as libmpq__archive_add_path(3), including distinct first- and later-sector compression masks; NULL selects default storage options. Supplied locale and platform must match the existing member or LIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT is returned. The original archive is not published until commit.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \fBLIBMPQ_SUCCESS\fP on success, or a negative libmpq error.
.SH ERRORS
A missing member returns LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST. A shared physical block, mismatched locale/platform, or unsupported storage options return LIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT. Source open/read, allocation, encoding, and I/O errors may also be returned.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq__update_replace_data (3),
.BR libmpq__update_commit (3)
